{
  "configuration_id": "config_025",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) achieved 0.639 acc, and config_003 (same but rna_only) achieved 0.591 acc, confirming that adding image modality helps (~+5%). config_006 shows resnet50 and imagenet_vit_l are roughly equivalent with pca_n2000. The largest remaining uncertainty is the RNA encoder: we have only tested pca_n2000 (linear, 2000-dim), while scvi_n200 (learned nonlinear, 200-dim) and scgpt (pre-trained generative) are untested. Question: config_025 (scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) changes ONLY the RNA encoder relative to config_001, cleanly isolating the effect of a learned nonlinear representation vs. PCA while holding image encoder, aggregation, fusion, and profile setting constant. Why this is the best next experiment: the RNA encoder is the most fundamental representation choice and appears across the majority of remaining configurations; knowing whether scvi_n200 outperforms or underperforms pca_n2000 will guide many subsequent decisions about which encoder family to pursue, and the single-variable design maximizes information per experiment under the limited budget."
}

